 done? Nope, just, just, just, thick, thick, just, thick, thick Now the hips sittin', now the booty pokin' Now the confidence showin', yeah Now when I walk in, heads keep turnin' Curse is cursin', baby, I got money now Link below","callToAction":"SHOP NOW","landingPageUrl":"https://shopamua.com/pages/curve-quiz","landingPageDomain":"shopamua.com","ctaDescription":"Embrace your curves, naturally","ctaLinkDescription":null},"metrics":{"reach":158480,"aggregatedReach":null,"estimatedSpend":1426,"duplicates":2,"reachDelta1d":null,"reachDelta7d":null,"reachDelta30d":null},"audience":{"targetedCountries":["GB","US"],"mainCountry":"GB","gender":null,"ageMin":null,"ageMax":null},"rank":{"positionInPage":1,"currentRank":1,"rankDelta":null,"improvementPct":0.5},"flags":{"isEuAd":null,"isLowReach":false,"isMediaChanged":true,"hasPartnerBadge":false}},{"id":"facebook_1940321336652313","collationId":"1597481931766633","platform":"facebook","status":"inactive","createdAt":"2026-08-02T03:10:33.581Z","firstSeenAt":"2026-07-31T07:00:00.000Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-08-03T07:00:00.000Z","daysRunning":3,"media":{"type":"video","thumbnailUrl":"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/thumbnails/ce2b82fc2018fe4b6feee1b185b33e6b0a4c28b9095056982c492062697efc5b.jpg","mediaUrl":"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/video/94a98304b30e028f44a3686e042a33e40605fd3feed5afa949ed4d4703fdf2fe.mp4"},"advertiser":{"id":"496995063506769","name":"Amua","logoUrl":"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/496995063506769.jpg","facebookPageId":"496995063506769","liveAdsCount":555,"reach30d":126886,"totalReach":2026434,"countriesCount":2,"facebookLikes":16382,"instagramFollowers":18803},"content":{"title":null,"body":"Feel confident in your body with a natural blend designed to support healthy weight gain in the right places!","transcript":"И","callToAction":"SHOP NOW","landingPageUrl":"https://shopamua.com/pages/curves-quizv2","landingPageDomain":"shopamua.com","ctaDescription":"Embrace your curves, naturally","ctaLinkDescription":null},"metrics":{"reach":116982,"aggregatedReach":null,"estimatedSpend":1053,"duplicates":2,"reachDelta1d":null,"reachDelta7d":null,"reachDelta30d":null},"audience":{"targetedCountries":["GB","US"],"mainCountry":"GB","gender":null,"ageMin":null,"ageMax":null},"rank":{"positionInPage":18,"currentRank":18,"rankDelta":null,"improvementPct":10.17},"flags":{"isEuAd":null,"isLowReach":false,"isMediaChanged":true,"hasPartnerBadge":false}},{"id":"facebook_1610595196830927","collationId":"1114496824520061","platform":"facebook","status":"active","createdAt":"2026-11-05T06:50:42.992Z","firstSeenAt":"2026-11-04T08:00:00.000Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-11-15T23:02:21.566Z","daysRunning":12,"media":{"type":"video","thumbnailUrl":"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/thumbnails/aefd2bd2d1c2b117deb8d192e67a1d4dd92827cbd4a8de0e2c4ca0367f349d84.jpg","mediaUrl":"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/video/370c0b94487f17f64fbecc8a06e7870bb8616c3e3ad500fa77afdb6bcf9b8983.mp4"},"advertiser":{"id":"1120223791172422","name":"Roseline William","logoUrl":"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/1120223791172422.jpg","facebookPageId":"1120223791172422","liveAdsCount":565,"reach30d":295225,"totalReach":1104995,"countriesCount":2,"facebookLikes":1657,"instagramFollowers":null},"content":{"title":null,"body":"Feel confident in your body with a natural blend designed to support healthy weight gain in the right places!","transcript":null,"callToAction":"SHOP NOW","landingPageUrl":"https://shopamua.com/products/amua-vitaldrops","landingPageDomain":"shopamua.com","ctaDescription":"Embrace your curves, naturally","ctaLinkDescription":null},"metrics":{"reach":106999,"aggregatedReach":null,"estimatedSpend":963,"duplicates":2,"reachDelta1d":2424,"reachDelta7d":39382,"reachDelta30d":86341},"audience":{"targetedCountries":["CA","GB"],"mainCountry":"GB","gender":null,"ageMin":null,"ageMax":null},"rank":{"positionInPage":14,"currentRank":14,"rankDelta":-1,"improvementPct":2.63},"flags":{"isEuAd":null,"isLowReach":false,"isMediaChanged":true,"hasPartnerBadge":false}},{"id":"facebook_1441696914452609","collationId":"1045584278224272","platform":"facebook","status":"inactive","createdAt":"2026-08-15T14:58:20.515Z","firstSeenAt":"2026-08-14T07:00:00.000Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-08-25T07:00:00.000Z","daysRunning":11,"media":{"type":"image","thumbnailUrl":null,"mediaUrl":"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/image/af6a94b110deaf12bdb4deea44deaa88fe3363284a1f1248fbcb2c6b32bb7ec4.png"},"advertiser":{"id":"1099905903209760","name":"Thick Girl Secrets","logoUrl":"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/1099905903209760.jpg","facebookPageId":"1099905903209760","liveAdsCount":54,"reach30d":18763,"totalReach":676791,"countriesCount":120,"facebookLikes":2738,"instagramFollowers":null},"content":{"title":null,"body":"My ex told me I was too skinny.\n\nNow he's in prison.\n\nBefore anybody starts typing:\n\nNO.\n\nI did not send him there because he insulted my body.\n\nThose are two completely separate events.\n\nI promise.\n\nBut the way life wrote that sequence of events is absolutely insane.\n\nAnd there's a much longer story behind this picture than anybody would ever guess.\n\n========\n\nThis man and I dated years ago.\n\nAnd the relationship itself was already on life support.\n\nYou know when you're technically together but you're both just irritating each other professionally?\n\nThat was us.\n\nEverything became an argument.\n\nWhere are you?\n\nWhy didn't you answer?\n\nWho is that?\n\nWhy did you say it like that?\n\nWhy did you breathe in that tone?\n\nExhausting.\n\n========\n\nOne night we got into a bad argument.\n\nI genuinely don't even remember what started it.\n\nProbably something stupid.\n\nBut eventually he said:\n\n“You're built like a little girl anyway.”\n\nAnd then made a comment about me having no butt.\n\nNow logically:\n\nThis man was angry.\n\nHe was saying whatever he thought would hurt.\n\nI understood that.\n\nBut unfortunately for me, he accidentally found the exact insecurity I had never told him about.\n\nAnd when somebody hits the insecurity you secretly already have?\n\nThat sentence sticks.\n\n========\n\nI acted like I didn't care.\n\nProbably said something back.\n\nWe broke up not long after.\n\nAnd I went around telling everybody:\n\n“I'm good.”\n\nI was NOT good.\n\nNot because I missed him.\n\nLet me make that clear.\n\nThat relationship needed to end.\n\nBut his comment stayed in my head.\n\nEvery time I got dressed.\n\nEvery time I saw myself from the side.\n\nEvery time I stood beside a curvier woman.\n\nEvery time jeans fit weird.\n\nThat stupid sentence came back.\n\n========\n\nI'd always been skinny.\n\nVery skinny growing up.\n\nAnd when I got older, I expected my body to eventually fill out.\n\nLike maybe one birthday I'd wake up and the hips department would finally open.\n\nNever happened.\n\nEarly twenties?\n\nStill straight.\n\nLater?\n\nStill straight.\n\nMy friends filled out.\n\nMy cousins filled out.\n\nI remained committed to the line segment.\n\n========\n\nAnd the issue wasn't that I wanted to become huge.\n\nI just wanted a womanly shape.\n\nMore hips.\n\nMore thighs.\n\nSomething in the back.\n\nI wanted to wear jeans and have them FIT.\n\nNot technically stay on my body.\n\nFit.\n\nThere's a difference.\n\n========\n\nAfter the breakup, wanting curves turned into an obsession.\n\nBecause now it wasn't only:\n\n“I want this.”\n\nIt became:\n\n“I need to prove him wrong.”\n\nWhich is a TERRIBLE reason to make decisions about your body.\n\nBut that's where I was mentally.\n\nI started eating more.\n\nA lot more.\n\nPeople always tell skinny girls:\n\n“Just eat.”\n\nAs if we're photosynthesizing before that.\n\nSo I ate.\n\nBreakfast.\n\nLunch.\n\nDinner.\n\nSnacks.\n\nDessert.\n\nEverything.\n\nI gained some weight.\n\nMostly stomach.\n\nIncredible.\n\nThank you, body.\n\nExactly the location requested.\n\n========\n\nThen the gym.\n\nI went HARD.\n\nPartially for me.\n\nPartially out of spite.\n\nAnd spite is actually a powerful pre-workout.\n\nHip thrusts.\n\nSquats.\n\nLunges.\n\nKickbacks.\n\nRDLs.\n\nEverything.\n\nI'd be in the gym thinking:\n\nOh he's going to REGRET IT.\n\nCompletely ridiculous.\n\nThis man was probably at home playing video games.\n\nMeanwhile I'm doing Bulgarian split squats in emotional distress.\n\n========\n\nThe gym absolutely changed my body somewhat.\n\nI got stronger.\n\nMy legs looked better.\n\nI enjoyed seeing progress.\n\nBut I was still naturally slim.\n\nStill struggled to keep weight on.\n\nStill wanted more fullness.\n\nThen came weight gain shakes.\n\nDifferent powders.\n\nRandom TikTok recommendations.\n\nEverything.\n\nIf somebody online said:\n\n“This made me thick.”\n\nI was listening.\n\nThat phase cost me an embarrassing amount of money.\n\n========\n\nEventually I realized something.\n\nI was letting somebody I didn't even LIKE anymore control how I felt about my body.\n\nThat's crazy.\n\nImagine ending a relationship with somebody but keeping their opinion on a monthly subscription.\n\nNo.\n\nCancel.\n\nSo I changed the goal.\n\nI still wanted curves.\n\nAbsolutely.\n\nBut now I wanted them because I liked that look for myself.\n\nNot to prove anything to him.\n\nThat mental difference was huge.\n\n========\n\nI simplified my routine.\n\nStarted eating more consistently instead of randomly stuffing myself for three days and then forgetting breakfast for a week.\n\nKept training.\n\nActually slept.\n\nStopped chasing every product somebody mentioned online.\n\nAnd that's eventually when I came across VitalDrops.\n\n========\n\nI had seen it before but ignored it.\n\nThen one night I ended up reading reviews.\n\nAnd what kept me reading was seeing women with naturally slim body types.\n\nWomen talking about exactly what I'd struggled with.\n\nEating but not seeing much change.\n\nTraining but wanting more overall shape.\n\nFeeling invisible next to curvier friends.\n\nThat felt familiar.\n\n========\n\nSo I researched it.\n\nWaited.\n\nWent back.\n\nRead more.\n\nThen ordered.\n\nMy expectation wasn't:\n\nI'm going to wake up next Thursday unrecognizable.\n\nAt that point I had been through enough internet nonsense.\n\nI simply wanted something I could add to the routine I was already committed to.\n\n========\n\nAnd then I did something extremely difficult for me:\n\nI stayed consistent.\n\nI didn't switch approaches after two weeks.\n\nVitalDrops stayed part of my daily routine.\n\nI kept eating.\n\nKept training.\n\nKept giving my body time.\n\nAnd I tried very hard not to inspect myself in the mirror every morning expecting breaking news.\n\n========\n\nAt first the changes were small.\n\nMy appetite.\n\nMy clothes.\n\nJeans getting snugger through areas that had always been loose.\n\nLeggings looking better.\n\nNothing dramatic enough that I'd trust my own opinion.\n\nBecause when you WANT something to change, you can convince yourself anything changed.\n\nSo I waited.\n\n========\n\nThen other people started saying things.\n\nThat mattered more.\n\nMy cousin:\n\n“Girl, you getting thick.”\n\nMy friend:\n\n“Okay BODY.”\n\nAnother friend asked whether I'd changed my gym routine.\n\nThat was when I finally allowed myself to believe I wasn't imagining everything.\n\n========\n\nAnd over time, I started feeling different in clothes.\n\nThat was huge.\n\nInstead of choosing outfits that HID my body, I started choosing clothes that showed it.\n\nFitted dresses.\n\nLeggings.\n\nJeans.\n\nStuff I used to avoid.\n\nI stopped doing that thing where you put on an outfit, like it for three seconds, then stare at yourself until you find something wrong and change.\n\n========\n\nAttention changed too.\n\nI know people hate admitting that this matters.\n\nI'll admit it.\n\nMen started noticing me differently.\n\nGuys who had known me for YEARS suddenly had a lot more eye contact.\n\nInteresting development.\n\nStrangers were friendlier.\n\nCompliments happened more.\n\nAnd yes, that did feel validating at first.\n\nBecause I had spent years being the one who felt overlooked.\n\n========\n\nBut eventually something even better happened:\n\nI stopped needing those reactions as proof.\n\nI liked how I looked before anybody said anything.\n\nThat is the actual win.\n\nBecause if confidence only exists when somebody is complimenting you, then you're still giving strangers control over it.\n\nI had already made that mistake once with my ex.\n\nI wasn't doing it again.\n\n========\n\nNow let's return to the prison situation.\n\nBecause I know that's why you're still reading.\n\nYears pass.\n\nI barely think about this man anymore.\n\nDifferent life.\n\nDifferent people.\n\nEverything.\n\nThen one day somebody we both know messages me.\n\nNormal conversation.\n\nEventually they casually mention:\n\n“You know ___ got locked up, right?”\n\nExcuse me?\n\nI thought they were joking.\n\nThey were not joking.\n\n========\n\nI started asking questions.\n\nAnd that's how I eventually saw that he really was incarcerated.\n\nThe man who once convinced me that my body wasn't good enough was now behind a fence while I was finally living a life where his opinion didn't matter.\n\nYou cannot write this stuff.\n\nLife's writers room was working overtime.\n\n========\n\nAnd before anybody asks:\n\nNo, I didn't go visit.\n\nNo, I didn't send a letter.\n\nNo, I did not dramatically walk past the prison wearing Fashion Nova.\n\nNothing like that.\n\nThe picture just reminds me of the whole story because prisons always make me think about the insane update.\n\n========\n\nThe real lesson wasn't:\n\n“Look at me now.”\n\nIt was:\n\nWhy did I ever let one angry sentence control me for years?\n\nThat's what I wish I could tell younger me.\n\nChange your body if YOU want to.\n\nWork on your confidence if YOU want to.\n\nWear what makes YOU happy.\n\nBut don't build your entire self-image around somebody else's opinion.\n\nEspecially somebody who may eventually be unavailable for comment during normal visiting hours.\n\nI'M SORRY.\n\n========\n\nVitalDrops is still something I use as part of my routine now.\n\nI combine it with consistent eating, training, and taking better care of myself overall.\n\nThat's the period where I finally started liking how my shape was developing instead of desperately chasing overnight results.\n\nThey're currently offering Buy 2, Get 1 Free.\n\nAnd there is a money-back guarantee if you're curious and want to see whether it makes sense for your own routine.\n\nEverybody's body is different, obviously.\n\nI'm just sharing what I personally added to mine.\n\n========\n\nAs for my ex?\n\nI genuinely don't hate the man.\n\nI hope he figures his life out.\n\nI hope he grows.\n\nI hope he becomes a better person.\n\nI hope he finds peace.\n\nI hope he uses this experience to reflect.\n\nAll of that.\n\nBut if somebody asks whether I occasionally remember:\n\n“You're built like a little girl anyway”\n\nwhile putting on leggings that fit VERY differently now?\n\nYes.\n\nYes I do.\nRespectfully.","transcript":null,"callToAction":"LEARN MORE","landingPageUrl":"https://shopamua.com/products/amua-vitaldrops","landingPageDomain":"shopamua.com","ctaDescription":"My ex said I was too skinny… now look","ctaLinkDescription":"Supports your natural curves with a 100% natural formula."},"metrics":{"reach":87220,"aggregatedReach":null,"estimatedSpend":785,"duplicates":3,"reachDelta1d":null,"reachDelta7d":null,"reachDelta30d":null},"audience":{"targetedCountries":["AE","AG","AI","AQ","AS","AT","AU","AW","AZ","BB","BE","BG","BH","BM","BN","BO","BS","BZ","CA","CC","CK","CL","CO","CW","CX","CY","CZ","DE","DK","DM","DO","EC","EE","ES","FI","FJ","FK","FM","FO","FR","GB","GD","GG","GI","GL","GP","GR","GU","GY","HR","HU","IE","IL","IM","IT","JE","JM","JO","KI","KN","KW","KY","LC","LT","LU","LV","MF","MH","MO","MP","MQ","MS","MT","MX","MY","NC","NF","NL","NR","NU","NZ","OM","PE","PL","PM