hat did you do? I don't know what you're talking about. Don't play dumb with me. I've seen your old photos. Why are you looking at my old photos? They're on his phone. He still has them. That sounds like a conversation for you and him. That's not the same body. I'm not stupid. You were flat, straight up and down. Now you're out here looking like that? What surgeon did you go to? I didn't have surgery. Stop lying. I'm not lying. BBL? No. Lipo and transfer? No. Then what? Because bodies don't just do that. Mine did. Why do you care? Because he can't stop looking at you. We've been together eight months and I've never seen him look at me like that. So I need to know what you did, please. It's drops. Drops? Under my tongue. Every morning. That's it? That's it. How does that even work? When women stress, our hormones shift. Body starts storing fat in the wrong places. Stomach, arms. The drops fix the signal. Remind your body where fat is supposed to go. Hips, thighs, behind. So nothing got added? Nothing got added. No surgery. No surgery. No injections. No recovery. How long before you saw results? Few weeks. But by month two, I couldn't fit my old jeans. Look, I'm not trying to take your man. I don't want him back. But if you're worried about how you look, that's on you to fix. Not me. What's it called? Why should I tell you? You locked me in a bathroom. I'm sorry. Okay? I just... He still has your photos. That messes with your head. Amua. A-M-U-A. Vital Drops. Is there a website? There's a link. I'll write it down. Thank you. Mm-hmm. And delete my photos off his phone. That's weird. Yeah. There you are. Where'd you go? Bathroom. You good? I'm good. You sure? I'm about to be better. What does that mean? Nothing. Let's go. My ex's new girlfriend locked me in a bathroom, got in my face, said he still has my old photos on his phone, said he couldn't stop staring at me. She thought I had surgery. I didn't. A-M-U-A Vital Drops.","callToAction":"SHOP NOW","landingPageUrl":"ht