\":2278,\"instagramFollowers\":10361},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"For almost two years I thought my hip pain was just something I had to live with.\\n\\nSleeping on my side hurt.\\n\\nStairs hurt.\\n\\nGetting out of bed every morning felt like a battle.\\n\\nI tried collagen, turmeric, physio, stretching, cortisone shots, and more ibuprofen than I'd like to admit.\\n\\nNothing lasted.\\n\\nThen I found out I had gluteal tendinopathy.\\n\\nWhat shocked me was learning it wasn't really a hip problem at all.\\n\\nIt was an estrogen problem.\\n\\nAfter menopause, estrogen drops and the tendons around your hips lose one of the things they've relied on for decades. They become weaker, stiffer, and more prone to irritation.\\n\\nThat's why so many women suddenly develop that burning pain on the outside of the hip.\\n\\nThe pillow between the knees.\\n\\nThe pain when rolling over in bed.\\n\\nThe stairs getting harder every month.\\n\\nThe thing that finally helped me was learning about moringa.\\n\\nMoringa contains plant compounds called phytoestrogens that support the same pathways estrogen used to support.\\n\\nI started using She Again because it contains a concentrated moringa extract instead of the weak doses found in teas and cheap capsules.\\n\\nAbout four weeks later I was sleeping on my side again.\\n\\nWalking comfortably again.\\n\\nOff the daily ibuprofen.\\n\\nAnd most importantly, I felt like myself again.\\n\\nIf you've been told your hip pain is just aging, it might be worth looking into gluteal tendinopathy and the role estrogen plays in tendon health.\",\"transcript\":null,\"callToAction\":\"LEARN MORE\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://www.hernovabottle.com/products/menopaused\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"hernovabottle.com\",\"ctaDescription\":\"How I Fixed My Gluteal Tendinopathy In 4 Weeks\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":null},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":87058,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":784,\"duplicates\":14,\"reachDelta1d\":126,\"reachDelt