{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HNNk14MnZrTrQJzzMh5cjP","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"requestId\":\"a9453ab1-c644-48e1-9016-4e47c80fcaf1\",\"data\":[{\"id\":\"facebook_979941251390313\",\"collationId\":\"960719690145510\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-11T22:21:48.669Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-11-11T08:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-11-13T00:16:14.019Z\",\"daysRunning\":5,\"media\":{\"type\":\"image\",\"thumbnailUrl\":null,\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/image/036ce5366350159b27cbcb6c8fdd44df004023c345cb0b78e3d25a46729e3df2.png\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"121865484174539\",\"name\":\"Hemokare\",\"logoUrl\":null,\"facebookPageId\":\"121865484174539\",\"liveAdsCount\":44,\"reach30d\":0,\"totalReach\":0,\"countriesCount\":1,\"facebookLikes\":490,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"My little sister asked me to be her maid of honor in March. The wedding was in September. I said yes before she finished the sentence.\\n\\nThen she sent the dress.\\n\\nBlush pink. Fitted. The kind of dress that's made for a body with curves. I put it on in my bedroom and stood in front of the mirror for a long time. It just hung on me. Flat in the back. Loose in the hips. Like it was waiting for somebody else to fill it out.\\n\\nI'm 31. I'm not out of shape. I walk every day. I'd been doing booty workouts from TikTok three times a week for almost a year. Squats, hip thrusts, the band around the knees. I was putting in the work. My jeans still fit exactly the same as they did the year before.\\n\\nI told my sister maybe I should get a different dress. She looked at me like I'd lost my mind. \\\"You're wearing the dress.\\\"\\n\\nMy cousin Tasha was the one who said something. We were at my aunt's house and she caught me tugging at my jeans in the hallway mirror. She asked what was wrong and I told her about the dress.\\n\\nShe didn't laugh. She said, \\\"Girl, you're training on empty.\\\"\\n\\nShe told me your glutes are the biggest muscle you have. And muscle runs on creatine. She said she'd been doing the same workouts for a year with nothing to show for it, until she started feeding the muscle instead of just working it.\\n\\nShe showed me what she takes. Peach Boost. Four gummies every morning. 4,000mg of creatine, plus collagen and BCAAs. Sugar-free. She said they taste like pink lemonade, and she was right about that too.\\n\\nI was skeptical. I've bought every \\\"booty\\\" product on the internet at least once. But they had a 60-day money-back guarantee, so the worst case was I'd send them back.\\n\\nI put the bottle next to my coffee maker. Four every morning. Same workouts. No skipping.\\n\\nThe first two weeks I didn't notice anything. I almost stopped.\\n\\nWeek three my workouts felt different. I wasn't dying by the last set. I could add another round of hip thrusts.\\n\\nWeek four I tried the dress on again. Just to check.\\n\\nIt fit different. Not a little. Different. The back of the dress actually had something to sit on. My sister walked in on me turning sideways in the mirror and just screamed.\\n\\nAt the wedding, three different women asked me what I'd been doing. One of them asked if I'd had something done. I hadn't. No surgery. No needles. No downtime. Just the same workouts and four gummies every morning.\\n\\nI'm not the only one hearing that question, either. Crystal T., a verified customer, wrote: \\\"I've already been questioned if I had a procedure.\\\"\\n\\nIf you've been doing the work and the mirror isn't moving, it might not be the work. It might be the fuel.\\n\\n👉 Tap the link to see the Peach Story.\\n\\nStory is illustrative. Names changed. Results vary and come with consistent daily use and exercise.\",\"transcript\":null,\"callToAction\":\"LEARN MORE\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://hemokare.com/pages/peach-story\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"hemokare.com\",\"ctaDescription\